# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Weights & Biases -------------------------------------------------------
# Live W&B run payloads are large and machine-written. Provenance lives in
# runs/<experiment_id>/resolved_config.json (which records wandb_run_id), so
# nothing scientific is lost by not tracking these.
wandb/
code/wandb/
!archive/**/wandb_runs_*/

# --- Per-run output directories (plan.md 2.2) -------------------------------
# runs/<experiment_id>/ IS the canonical record, so the small provenance and
# metric files ARE tracked (updated_rules.md 9: every figure must be traceable
# to exact run IDs). Only the large or regenerable payloads are excluded.
runs/**/checkpoint.pt
runs/**/*.pt
runs/**/stdout.log

# --- Model checkpoints outside the archive ----------------------------------
# The two checkpoints under archive/pre_finalization/ are tracked as evidence of
# the pre-audit state and are unaffected by this rule.
#
# T11.5: the exception is scoped to `pre_finalization` deliberately. It used to
# read `!archive/**/*.pt`, which was correct when those two files were the only
# archived checkpoints -- but `archive/t9_1_undeclared_group_runs/` and
# `archive/t10_smoke_1epoch/` later added 11 more, ~155 MB, and the blanket
# exception would have committed all of them. Those runs are INVALIDATED; the
# evidence a future reader needs is their `config.json`,
# `resolved_config.json`, `metrics.json`, `results.tsv` and
# `INVALIDATED.md` -- all still tracked. A checkpoint of an invalidated run is
# not citable and is regenerable from its own recorded config, so it is weight,
# not evidence. The files remain on disk; only tracking is declined.
*.pt
!archive/pre_finalization/**/*.pt

# --- Global output filenames that Phase 0 abolished -------------------------
# Listed so a stray legacy write is never committed by accident.
/best_model.pt
/results.tsv
/final_run_metrics.json
/sweep_results.csv
/1block_results.csv
/2block_results.csv
code/best_model.pt
code/results.tsv
code/final_run_metrics.json

# --- Gate smoke runs (T-L0.3b) ----------------------------------------------
# Gate 5 LAUNCHES two real 1-epoch training runs so that its provenance and
# metric-contract checks grade a directory produced by the code under test rather
# than whichever archived run sorted last by mtime. That is deliberate and is what
# fixed T-L0.3b -- but it means every execution of the suite deposits a fresh
# `__rN` directory, and the suite is expected to run after every commit (T-LX.0).
#
# These are regenerable gate artifacts, not evidence: nothing cites them, they are
# 1-epoch proxies that may never enter a table, and the next suite run recreates
# them. Tracking them would grow the repository without bound in exchange for
# nothing citable. This is NOT a deletion (CLAUDE.md 6) -- the directories stay on
# disk; only tracking is declined, exactly as for invalidated checkpoints above.
#
# `runs/t_l03_mor_timing_seed44__fa9339bc` is deliberately NOT covered: the
# changelog cites it as the run on which the eleven-key `"N/A"` metric contract was
# verified at HEAD, so it is evidence and is tracked.
runs/t67_provenance_check*/
runs/t67d_provenance_check*/

# --- Editor / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
